 {"id":"INFRA-LORE-044","title":"[P4] Guard hook budget defaults below its own test timeout — every commit carries a fail-open warning","status":"complete","priority":"P4","created_by":null,"reasoning":"Measured 2026-11-21 on main 8ec0c83: every commit prints 'WARN: hook_timeout=300s <= test_timeout=1200s in /home/kara/get-h3/lore: the guard would be cut off mid-run and report a fail-open PASS. Raising this run's budget to 1320s'. The repo declares evaluator.test_timeout 600 (.gitreins/config.yaml line 40) but declares no guards.hook_timeout, so the hook budget falls back to a 300s default while the guard itself computes a 1200s effective test timeout. The guard works around it per run, which means the warning is perpetual and the declared-vs-effective gap is never closed: a slow box can still end the hook before the test lane finishes and the commit then reads PASS on a run that never completed. Pre-existing; not caused by any 2026-11-20/21 change. Fix is config-only: declare a hook timeout above the effective test timeout so the guard's own arithmetic stops warning.","detail":{"fingerprint":"a2a18c49ae0ba247461cc310b94c412b936defac7320462570f9e726a1d2a180","evidence":[{"run_id":"c6d966fa","ts":"2026-11-21T04:04:20Z"}]},"source":null,"acceptance_criteria":"1. The guard's hook budget is declared rather than defaulted: `git grep -c hook_timeout .gitreins/config.yaml` prints a number greater than 0; expect the declared value to exceed the effective test timeout the guard reports.\n2. A board-only commit's guard log carries no fail-open warning: commit a board-only change and expect no line pairing hook_timeout with a smaller number than test_timeout.\n3. Declared and effective test timeouts agree: the guard log's reported test timeout equals the value declared in the config; expect one number, never two.\n4. The guard still reaches a real verdict on a full test run: commit a code change and expect the guard's test lane to report passed tests, not a timeout, at the declared budget.\nGATE ARM: Run `git grep -c hook_timeout .gitreins/config.yaml`; expect a number greater than 0.\n","capability_tags":[],"complexity":1,"created_at":"2026-11-21T01:11:25Z","updated_at":"2026-11-21T04:04:20Z","worker_status":"complete","commit_hash":"75c094b91ef8bd5837a7c4f94887c87d7ec4fcb9","guard_result":"PASS","ci_result":"GREEN","completed_at":null,"worktree":"/home/kara/worktrees/lore-INFRA-LORE-044","branch":"wt/INFRA-LORE-044","worker_summary":"Merge 75c094b of wt/INFRA-LORE-044 (worker commits: probes 8faab64/a95845c + fix a556d76 + foreman comment correction 3614f44; cx/gpt-6.1-terra@9router). guards.test_timeout 1200 + guards.hook_timeout 1320 replace evaluator.test_timeout 600 (unknown key under gitreins 0.21.x; schema accepts both under guards per config_schema.py:117-118; unset defaults are tests 1200s / hook 300s per guard_manager.py:1783/1790). RED: pre-fix probe commit printed the unknown-key WARN (worktree log T034124; foreman's 3766e21 board commit printed it on main). GREEN: post-merge probe commit on main printed no warnings (log T035229); live GuardManager on the fixed config emits empty stderr; config validate_config_file issue count 0. Judge caveat honored: branch GREEN probe a95845c shared the pre-fix tree (empty diff vs 8faab64) - the real transition is a556d76 + warning-free post-merge main. Gates on graded tree 75c094b91ef8bd5837a7c4f94887c87d7ec4fcb9: 572 passed, ruff clean, format clean, count guard PASS. Tier-2 verdict PASS/COMPLETE, history run 2026-11-21/c6d966fa (stdout id 51466834).","foreman_note":null,"type":null}
 {"id":"LORE-EXPORT-1","status":"complete","priority":"P2","type":"feature","title":"P2 — export lore gate runs as a Prometheus textfile gauge so h3 can observe them (h3 row H3-OBS-05 arm A was split out to here)","reasoning":"WHY THIS ROW EXISTS (filed by the h3 PM lane, tick h3-pm-2026-11-21-09-07-34): h3 row H3-OBS-05 requires `grep -c '^lore_gate_runs_total' /var/lib/node_exporter/textfile/h3_lore.prom` >= 1. Measured on the box at 2026-11-21T10:20Z: `ls /var/lib/node_exporter/textfile/h3_lore.prom` => No such file, while the sibling exporter h3_verify.prom exists with 9 gauge series. The producer named by that h3 arm is `python -m lore gate`, i.e. THIS repo's CLI, so the deliverable is lore-side and an h3 worker cannot satisfy it. The lore board held zero open rows when this was filed, so nothing tracked the exporter.\n\nSURFACE: `lore gate` CLI (and whatever internal runner it calls) in /home/kara/get-h3/lore.\nREADER: h3's observability chain — node_exporter textfile collector -> Prometheus -> the h3 dashboards/alerts that are supposed to show gate health. Until this exports, the h3_lore_* family is simply absent, which is indistinguishable from 'no gate ever ran'.\n\nSCOPE (do not scope-creep): one gauge family emitted on every gate run. Do not add an HTTP endpoint, do not change gate semantics, do not touch h3_verify.prom (another producer owns it).","acceptance_criteria":"1) One `python -m lore gate` invocation writes /var/lib/node_exporter/textfile/h3_lore.prom atomically (temp file in the same dir + os.replace) and the file contains at least one series named `lore_gate_runs_total` — verified by `grep -c '^lore_gate_runs_total' /var/lib/node_exporter/textfile/h3_lore.prom` returning >= 1.\n2) The value is a real counter, not a constant: two consecutive runs leave the second value exactly one greater than the first — quote both `grep '^lore_gate_runs_total' ...` readings in the row.\n3) Failure is loud, not silent: if the textfile directory is not writable